MBSA adaptations
  Prepared routing, Fixed/Remote orchestration and state merging retain the
  native Index multiplication path, without software operand decoding or
  scalar boundary recomputation. Hopper kernels are package-specific code
  using CUTLASS CuTe DSL and QuACK dependencies; the FP8 Indexer uses native
  mma.sync FP32 accumulation. Main Attention requires Maxwell geometry.
  Blackwell import/JIT compatibility changes preserve attributed arithmetic,
  masks, synchronization and stores. The CUDA CSR extension is named
  mbsa_build_k2q_csr_ext to avoid conflicts with other installations.

